      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VERBIL (3) is a genuine type who looks ready to peak this afternoon. Ran a better race last start at the fourth run back, getting home well but finding one better over this course and distance. Backs up seven days later with McDonald going on - strong signs that he is ready to win. KOMODO DRAGON (5) led all the way for comfortable victory over 1250m at the Kenso two back then went to Brisbane and struggled after getting back in the field over today's trip. Should punch forward from gate one and is a great chance to ping back into form. STALLONE (8) shouldered 61kgs but dominated in front at Hawkesbury recently. Far tougher ask today but with 5kgs less he can run another cheeky race. NAINA (9) drops 5kgs on a strong fourth over a similar trip at Caulfield recently. Nicely placed to play a key role. FELIX MAJESTIC (2) has strung together five minor placings but has not won since December 2023. Happy to throw him in the exotics.",
